{"user": "How does this game work?", "user_ts": "2026-08-18T16:34:41.033738+00:00", "assistant": "Othello/Reversi basics:\n\n- You play **Black**; the AI is **White**.\n- On your turn, you place a disc on a **legal square** \u2014 here those are marked by pale dots.\n- A move is legal if it **traps one or more White discs in a straight line** between your new Black disc and another Black disc.\n- Trapped White discs are then **flipped to Black**.\n- Lines can be horizontal, vertical, or diagonal.\n- If a player has **no legal move**, they must **pass**.\n- When the board is full, or neither player can move, the player with **more discs wins**.\n\nIn this position Black may play **a1, g2, or a3**. Since this is the endgame, don\u2019t just look for the move that flips the most now \u2014 think about who gets the last moves, corners, and whether you leave White good replies.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-18T16:34:43.987766+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-18T16:34:46.954711+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "General Principle", "Hint"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "General Principle", "Hint"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Hint": 2, "Local Justification": 1}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Hint": 0.6666666666666666, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "General Principle", "Hint"], "llama": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint